HST Office: HST Slides' Home and Insert tabs follow the approved 1.0.2 mockup (owner, 16/11/2026 02:14).

Home:
- Clipboard: Paste large over the three rows, Cut, Copy and Format Painter (moved from Font) in a labelled column;
  Paste Special is in the Paste drop-down.
- Slides: New Slide large, Duplicate and Delete (short labels, the tooltip keeps the full name) in a labelled column.
- Font and Paragraph: two rows of icons. Font: font, size, grow, shrink, change case, clear formatting / bold,
  italic, underline, strikethrough, shadow, subscript, superscript, spacing, highlight, color. Paragraph:
  bullets, numbering, decrease and increase indent, line spacing / the four alignments, beside a column of Text
  Direction and Align Text (a drop-down of the three vertical alignments) on the same two rows. Hanging indent,
  left-to-right, right-to-left and paragraph spacing leave the tab (Format menu, sidebar, paragraph dialog).
- Layouts (new group gdHomeHstLayouts, between Paragraph and Drawing): the slide layouts of AssignLayout.
- Drawing: Shapes large; Arrange (order, alignment and grouping in one drop-down), Fill and Outline labelled.
- Editing: Find, Replace and Select in one labelled column.
Insert: Text holds Text Box, Header and Footer, Fontwork, Date and Time, Slide Number and Other Object as large
buttons (the five unlabelled Fontwork and vertical text icons leave the tab); Symbols shows Equation before Symbol.

Groups of three rows put a large button over rows 0 to 2, small buttons in rows 0 to 2 and the caption in row 3.
New strings have an empty Vietnamese msgstr here; l10n/vi-overrides.jsonl holds their translations. The new menu
items and the Duplicate and Delete buttons take their labels from their commands (gla11y suppressions, as for the
other menus of this file).

